      "font" : "CMBX10",
      "font size" : 9.963,
      "text color" : "[0.0]",
      "content" : "Example 3 (Roy Model) In the Roy model, individuals self-select into treatment when their beneﬁts from the treatment are greater than nonpecuniary costs for treatment participation. The extended Roy model assumes that the nonpecuniary cost is deterministic with the following selection equation:",
      "kids" : [ {
        "type" : "paragraph",
        "pdfua_tag" : "P",
        "id" : 1,
        "page number" : 1,
        "bounding box" : [ 246.41, 242.03, 365.591, 259.315 ],
        "font" : "CMMI10",
        "font size" : 9.963,
        "text color" : "[0.0]",
        "content" : "D = 1{Y1 − Y0 ≥ µC (Z)},"
      }, {
        "type" : "paragraph",
        "pdfua_tag" : "P",
        "id" : 2,
        "page number" : 1,
        "bounding box" : [ 72.0, 165.634, 540.0, 222.529 ],
        "font" : "CMTI10",
        "font size" : 9.963,
        "text color" : "[0.0]",
        "content" : "where µC (Z) represents nonpecuniary costs with a vector of observables Z. Then treated (D = 1) and untreated people (D = 0) are the observed groups satisfying support restrictions {Y1 − Y0 ≥ µC (Z)} and {Y1 − Y0 < µC (Z)}, respectively."
      } ]
    }, {
      "type" : "list item",
      "pdfua_tag" : "LI",
      "page number" : 1,
      "bounding box" : [ 72.0, 122.886, 539.996, 152.778 ],
      "font" : "CMBX10",
      "font size" : 9.963,
      "text color" : "[0.0]",
      "content" : "Example 4 (DTE conditional on Potential Outcomes) The conditional DTE for the unobservable subgroup whose potential outcomes belong to a certain set C is written as",
      "kids" : [ ]
    } ]
